# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Critical concepts {#critical-concepts}"
msgstr "Konsep kritikal {#critical-concepts}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum information cannot be copied or \"cloned\".\n"
msgstr "Maklumat kuantum tidak boleh disalin atau \"diklon\".\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "You *can* repeat the same preparation process to make an ensemble of quantum states which are all the same, or nearly the same.\n"
msgstr "Anda *boleh* mengulangi proses persediaan yang sama untuk membuat ensembel keadaan kuantum yang semuanya sama, atau hampir sama.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An encryption/decryption key (a one-time pad) can be shared between two friends using quantum states.\n"
msgstr "Kunci penyulitan/penyahsulitan (pad sekali-guna) boleh dikongsi antara dua rakan menggunakan keadaan kuantum.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two friends randomly choosing a measurement basis means that half the time they will choose differently, and will have to toss out the information on those qubits.\n"
msgstr "Dua rakan yang memilih asas pengukuran secara rawak bermakna separuh daripada masa mereka akan memilih secara berbeza, dan perlu membuang maklumat pada qubit tersebut.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The random choice of measurement basis also ensures that an eavesdropper cannot know the initial state prepared, and thus cannot recreate the sent state. This ensures that the eavesdropping will be detected.\n"
msgstr "Pilihan asas pengukuran secara rawak juga memastikan penyadap tidak boleh mengetahui keadaan awal yang disediakan, dan dengan itu tidak boleh mencipta semula keadaan yang dihantar. Ini memastikan penyadapan akan dikesan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F questions {#tf-questions}"
msgstr "Soalan B/S {#tf-questions}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F In quantum key distribution, the two communicating partners measure each qubit in the same basis.\n"
msgstr "B/S Dalam pengagihan kunci kuantum, dua rakan berkomunikasi mengukur setiap qubit dalam asas yang sama.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F An eavesdropper intercepting quantum information in QKD is prevented by the laws of nature from copying the quantum state they intercept.\n"
msgstr "B/S Penyadap yang memintas maklumat kuantum dalam QKD dihalang oleh undang-undang alam daripada menyalin keadaan kuantum yang mereka pintas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F A one-time pad is a key for encrypting/decrypting secure messages in which a particular encoding scheme is used only once, for a single piece of information (like one letter of the alphabet).\n"
msgstr "B/S Pad sekali-guna adalah kunci untuk menyulitkan/menyahsulit mesej selamat di mana skim pengekodan tertentu hanya digunakan sekali, untuk satu keping maklumat (seperti satu huruf abjad).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "MC questions {#mc-questions}"
msgstr "Soalan aneka pilihan {#mc-questions}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Select the option that best completes the statement. As described in this module, a one-time pad is a set of encryption/decryption keys that is used...\n"
msgstr "Pilih pilihan yang paling melengkapkan pernyataan. Seperti yang diterangkan dalam modul ini, pad sekali-guna adalah satu set kunci penyulitan/penyahsulitan yang digunakan...\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "a. Only once for a single piece of information, like a single letter.\n"
msgstr "a. Hanya sekali untuk satu keping maklumat, seperti satu huruf.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "b. Only once for a single message.\n"
msgstr "b. Hanya sekali untuk satu mesej.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "c. Only once for a set period of time, like a day.\n"
msgstr "c. Hanya sekali untuk tempoh masa tertentu, seperti sehari.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "d. Until there is evidence of eavesdropping.\n"
msgstr "d. Sehingga ada bukti penyadapan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Assume Alice and Bob choose their measurement bases randomly. They measure. Then they share their measurement bases, and keep only the bits of information from cases where they used the same basis. Up to some random fluctuation, approximately what percentage of their qubits should yield usable bits of information?\n"
msgstr "Anggap Alice dan Bob memilih asas pengukuran mereka secara rawak. Mereka mengukur. Kemudian mereka berkongsi asas pengukuran mereka, dan menyimpan hanya bit maklumat daripada kes di mana mereka menggunakan asas yang sama. Sehingga beberapa turun naik rawak, kira-kira berapa peratus qubit mereka harus menghasilkan bit maklumat yang boleh digunakan?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "a. 100%\n"
msgstr "a. 100%\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "b. 50%\n"
msgstr "b. 50%\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "c. 25%\n"
msgstr "c. 25%\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "d. 12.5%\n"
msgstr "d. 12.5%\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "e. 0%\n"
msgstr "e. 0%\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "After Alice and Bob select cases in which they used the same measurement bases, what percentage of those bits of information should match, if quantum noise and errors were negligible?\n"
msgstr "Selepas Alice dan Bob memilih kes di mana mereka menggunakan asas pengukuran yang sama, berapa peratus bit maklumat tersebut harus sepadan, jika hingar dan ralat kuantum boleh diabaikan?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Assume Alice has chosen her measurement bases randomly. Eve also chooses her bases randomly, and she listens in (measures). She sends states on to Bob that are consistent with her measurements. Alice and Bob compare basis choices and keep only the qubits measured/prepared by them in the same bases. Up to some random fluctuation, approximately what percentage of those kept qubit measurements will match, according to Alice and Bob?\n"
msgstr "Anggap Alice telah memilih asas pengukurannya secara rawak. Eve juga memilih asasnya secara rawak, dan dia mendengar (mengukur). Dia menghantar keadaan kepada Bob yang konsisten dengan pengukurannya. Alice dan Bob membandingkan pilihan asas dan menyimpan hanya qubit yang diukur/disediakan oleh mereka dalam asas yang sama. Sehingga beberapa turun naik rawak, kira-kira berapa peratus pengukuran qubit yang disimpan itu akan sepadan, menurut Alice dan Bob?\n"

